<p>Italian government and sports officials on Thursday rejected a suggestion by Paolo Zampolli, a U.S. special envoy and Italian native, that Italy should take Iran’s place at the 2026 FIFA World Cup in North America. The idea gained attention after Zampolli said he had raised it with President Trump and FIFA President Gianni Infantino, arguing that he wanted to see Italy at a tournament hosted in part by the United States. Italian officials across politics and sport said qualification must be earned on the field, not handed out through politics, after Italy failed to qualify by losing a playoff on penalties to Bosnia and Herzegovina. Iran’s embassy in Rome also criticized the proposal, while Infantino said in mid-April that Iran “has to come” to the competition, signaling no support for any change. For readers, the clearest takeaway is simple: despite the diplomatic noise, Italy is publicly defending sporting merit, and FIFA’s lineup remains unchanged.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/kDg3dSgtsSZ9zAEQEStP2FxbWGS-95AktJ6GQgMKsmAdkA-g8fa6eKfumbWDgu0vnPHzHNZIyOlQ8_O89P0Vg9dnQZR_K0M83t9f6smuHqV5Aou6ceKt708d-bnfO19rxLM4yrmMkVQpk-GvftHLqBVrI98P3FFmc8SgwyKHmHn64ZtJlierlrHiHk8TgEwqW80uQHWAMwuIB0A-irDhU8jeciKJFew_qux71AdPZPN3ytxrXZW9X--eVwoD_AwgqjLfr7Yo1FAAdv9nTA' alt='U.S. Special Representative for Global Partnerships Paolo Zampolli in Belgrade on Tuesday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Minister response: Italian Sports Minister Andrea Abodi said giving Italy “a second chance” was “not appropriate” because teams must qualify “on the pitch”</li><li>Iran reaction: Iran’s embassy in Rome said “football belongs to the people, not to politicians” and accused the United States of trying to keep Iran out of the tournament</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Italian government: Sports Minister Andrea Abodi rejected the idea on sporting grounds, saying World Cup places must be won through qualifying, not reassigned through politics. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/world-cup-fifa-italy-participating-instead-of-iran/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Iran embassy in Rome: The embassy said football should stay separate from politics and argued that the U.S. push to remove Iran showed fear of Iran’s national team appearing at the tournament. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/world-cup-fifa-italy-participating-instead-of-iran/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Paolo Zampolli: Zampolli said he lobbied President Trump and FIFA leadership because, as an Italian-born U.S. envoy, he wanted to see Italy playing at a U.S.-hosted World Cup. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/sport/football/article/3351204/fifa-world-cup-italy-underwhelmed-trump-envoys-suggestion-they-should-replace-iran'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>FIFA leadership: Gianni Infantino said in mid-April that Iran “has to come” to the tournament, a sign that FIFA was not backing the proposed switch. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/world-cup-fifa-italy-participating-instead-of-iran/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/sport/football/article/3351204/fifa-world-cup-italy-underwhelmed-trump-envoys-suggestion-they-should-replace-iran'>Fifa World Cup: Italy underwhelmed by Trump envoy’s suggestion they should replace Iran</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/world-cup-fifa-italy-participating-instead-of-iran/'>Giving Italy second chance at FIFA World Cup ‘is not right’, sports minister says</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/sports/soccer/article-italy-trump-envoy-iran-war-soccer-world-cup/'>Italians quick to reject Trump envoy’s suggestion that team should replace Iran at World Cup</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/23/trump-envoy-calls-on-fifa-to-replace-iran-with-italy-at-world-cup'>Italian officials roundly reject proposal to replace Iran squad at 2026 World Cup</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://ww